<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert III, Duke of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1443–1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Albert the Bold</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert III, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a>, called the Bold, founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albertine-line">Albertine line</a> of the Wettin house when he and his brother Ernest divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> in 1485. A leading general of Emperor Maximilian I, he was named hereditary governor of Friesland in 1498 and imposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> rule on the Frisians, ending the Frisian Freedom west of the Ems. He died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emden">Emden</a> in 1500.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-iii-duke-of-saxony.jpg" alt="Albert III, Duke of Saxony" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albrecht_der_Beherzte,_1443-1500_(AT_KHM_GG4796).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
